.TH CB_GET_KV_EX 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
cb_get_kv_ex \- Extract the value from a key-value pair and return it as a pointer

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/cb_internal.h>
.IB #include <lib/str.h>

.IB void
.IB cb_get_kv_ex (
.IB void* kv,
.IB void** value
.IB );

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBcb_get_kv_ex\fR function extracts the value from a key-value pair and sets the provided pointer to point to the value.

The function takes two arguments:
.TP
.IR kv (void*)
A pointer to the key-value pair.
.TP
.IR value (void**)
A pointer to a pointer where the value will be stored.

The function does not return any value.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBcb_get_kv_ex\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/cb_internal.h>
#include <lib/str.h>

int main() {
    const char* kv = "key:value";
    void* value;

    cb_get_kv_ex((void*)kv, &value);

    printf("Value: %s\n", (char*)value);

    return 0;
}
.nef